<title>VENEZUELA: Andean Development Corp approves $226mln new loans.</title>
<headline>Andean Development Corp approves $226mln new loans.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Andean Development Corp (CAF), the financial arm of the Andean Community, said on Thursday that it approved a $226 million in new loans to member countries.</p>
<p>The biggest recipient was Venezuela for which the CAF set aside $60 million to partially finance a water treatment project and $50 million for a gold project led by Canada's Placer Dome. Brazil became the first CAF member outside of the Andean community to receive financing with an $86 million loan to improve roads between Brazil's northeast and Venezuela's southeast.</p>
<p>Other smaller loans were set aside for regional infrastructure, energy and business projects, the CAF said in a release. The CAF is an international financial institution made up of the five Andean Community countries -- Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Venezuela -- and four shareholders Brazil, Chile, Mexico and Trinidad and Tobago.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 834405</p>
